{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3223","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3223","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3223\",\"parent_revision\":\"11b8fdfb7a10e9c920947a057ef075abe1e661f4\",\"root_revision\":\"268268d64e4ea070571e3b958b62a2930cc7c3de98caab6b0cafeb7b4027e331\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-24\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPR #3207 (plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review) added the `review-synthesizer` agent and a new T5 synthesis dispatch stage to the multi-perspective-review skill. `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` was left unchanged, so it still shows the obsolete four-worker topology with no `review-synthesizer`, `synthesis-worker`, or Punch List node.\\n\\nPer `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md`, this is a Tier 2 change (new agent dispatched, new Mermaid forks in a SKILL.md) requiring re-extraction of the G4 (concurrency/dispatch topology) and L0/L1 (forks/traces) layers before `assemble_graph.py` can rebuild the graph. Both COVERAGE.md and `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` state that single-pass extraction is prohibited (data must go through the 3-worker ensemble + `reduce.py` corroboration + sonnet-reducer assembly pattern) and that the dedicated `dh:workflow-extractor` agent that used to run this is retired, with re-extraction \\\"pending redesign\\\" (see `docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md`).\\n\\nBecause the extraction mechanism itself is pending redesign, this could not be done as part of PR #3207 without either hand-editing the layer JSON (explicitly prohibited by COVERAGE.md's \\\"What NOT to do\\\") or running an unvalidated single-pass extraction (explicitly prohibited by workflow-extraction.md's trust boundary rule).\\n\\nUser-provided context: once `dh:workflow-extractor`'s replacement exists (see the PRD), re-run it against `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` and `plugins/development-harness/agents/review-synthesizer.md` to regenerate G4 (and L0/L1 for the new forks), then run `uv run plugins/development-harness/docs/assemble_graph.py` to rebuild `dh-workflow-graph.json`.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T16:34:09.982085Z</sub>\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"`docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` still shows the obsolete four-worker topology with no `review-synthesizer`, `synthesis-worker`, or Punch List node.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"Grep found zero matches for 'review-synthesizer', 'synthesis-worker', or 'Punch List' in the JSON file.\\\"\\n  source: \\\"`plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`; grep -E 'review-synthesizer|synthesis-worker|Punch List' returned no results\\\"\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"PR #3207 added the `review-synthesizer` agent and a new T5 synthesis dispatch stage to the multi-perspective-review skill.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"`review-synthesizer.md` agent file exists; multi-perspective-review SKILL.md contains 'T5', 'review-synthesizer', 'synthesis-worker', and 'Punch List' references as dispatch and task naming.\\\"\\n  source: \\\"`plugins/development-harness/agents/review-synthesizer.md` (exists); `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` contains T5 stage and synthesis-worker agent reference (grep output shows T5 task id, agent reference, Punch List section name)\\\"\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"Per `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md`, this is a Tier 2 change requiring re-extraction of the G4 and L0/L1 layers.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"COVERAGE.md lines 86\u2013101 document the Tier 2 update process: 'Source skill/agent files changed (SKILL.md, reference files, hooks.json)' requires re-extraction of affected layers (L0, L1, G4 per the table). T5 synthesis dispatch is a new agent dispatch, matching the Tier 2 pattern for 'New agent dispatched'.\\\"\\n  source: \\\"`plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md`, lines 86\u2013101 (Tier 2 table)\\\"\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"The dedicated `dh:workflow-extractor` agent that used to run this is retired, with re-extraction 'pending redesign'.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"Both COVERAGE.md (line 102) and workflow-extraction.md (line 28) contain the phrase 'pending redesign' with reference to the PRD. workflow-extraction.md explicitly states 'Extraction agents are pending redesign (see the PRD at [../../docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md](../../docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md)).' The PRD itself exists but its Status line (line 3) reads 'Draft v4 amended \u2014 fact-checked 2026-06-16; five design decisions resolved 2026-06-19' \u2014 still in Draft status, not shipped.\\\"\\n  source: \\\"`plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md`, line 102; `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md`, line 28; `plugins/development-harness/docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md`, line 3\\\"\\n\\n- verdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\n  claim: \\\"Single-pass extraction is prohibited (data must go through the 3-worker ensemble + `reduce.py` corroboration + sonnet-reducer assembly pattern). The ensemble dispatcher scripts (`dh-extract-file.js`, `reduce.py`) exist as the key open question: is the described blocker still real, or has the tooling since been built?\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"VERIFIED: The prohibition on single-pass extraction is explicitly stated in workflow-extraction.md lines 14\u201322: '3 haiku workers extract independently...`reduce.py --keep-threshold 2` corroborates...A sonnet reducer assembles'. VERIFIED: `reduce.py` exists at `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py`. VERIFIED: Helper scripts `enumerate_scope.py` and `merge_layer.py` exist in `plugins/development-harness/scripts/`. REFUTED: Main dispatcher `dh-extract-file.js` does NOT exist (searched entire dh plugin directory; only Python scripts found, no .js files matching this pattern). workflow-extractor-reducer.md agent references being dispatched 'by dh-extract-file.js', but that file is not present in the repo.\\\"\\n  source: \\\"`plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md`, lines 14\u201322 (rule statement); `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` (exists, confirmed via file listing); `plugins/development-harness/scripts/enumerate_scope.py` and `merge_layer.py` (both exist); `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor-reducer.md` (references dh-extract-file.js as dispatcher); find command result: dh-extract-file.js NOT FOUND in repo\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T16:44:28.529034Z</sub>\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"`docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` still shows obsolete four-worker topology with no `review-synthesizer`, `synthesis-worker`, or Punch List node.\\\"\\n  evidence: Grep found zero matches for these three terms in the JSON file.\\n  source: `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"PR #3207 added `review-synthesizer` agent and T5 synthesis dispatch stage.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"`review-synthesizer.md` exists; multi-perspective-review SKILL.md contains T5, review-synthesizer, synthesis-worker, Punch List references.\\\"\\n  source: `plugins/development-harness/agents/review-synthesizer.md`; `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md`\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"Tier 2 change requiring G4 and L0/L1 re-extraction per COVERAGE.md.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"COVERAGE.md lines 86\u2013101 document Tier 2 process; new agent dispatch matches pattern in the Tier 2 change table.\\\"\\n  source: `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md` lines 86\u2013101\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"`dh:workflow-extractor` retired, re-extraction pending redesign.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"COVERAGE.md line 102 and workflow-extraction.md line 28 both state 'pending redesign'. PRD exists but Status remains 'Draft v4' (dated 2026-06-19), not shipped.\\\"\\n  source: `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md` line 102; `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` line 28; `plugins/development-harness/docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md` line 3\\n\\n- verdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\n  claim: \\\"Single-pass extraction prohibited; ensemble + reduce.py + dispatcher scripts (dh-extract-file.js, reduce.py) exist.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"\u2713 VERIFIED: Prohibition explicit in workflow-extraction.md lines 14\u201322. \u2713 VERIFIED: reduce.py exists at `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py`. \u2713 VERIFIED: enumerate_scope.py and merge_layer.py exist in `plugins/development-harness/scripts/`. \u2717 REFUTED: Main dispatcher dh-extract-file.js NOT FOUND in repo\u2014workflow-extractor-reducer.md references it but the file is missing.\\\"\\n  source: `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` lines 14\u201322; `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` (confirmed via ls); `plugins/development-harness/scripts/enumerate_scope.py` and `merge_layer.py` (confirmed); `find` across dh plugin: dh-extract-file.js NOT FOUND\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T16:00:40.385597Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: unbounded-design\\n\\n**Rationale**: The derived artifact `dh-workflow-graph.json` requires regeneration following PR #3207's source changes (new review-synthesizer agent + T5 stage). The work is not a behavioral defect (system functions correctly) nor a recurring failure pattern. The blocker is the incomplete design of the workflow-extractor tool itself, which is documented as \\\"pending redesign\\\" in `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` and the PRD. The mechanical rebuild task is deferred until the tool design exists to implement it and establish automated gates for future drift prevention.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Decision tree traversal with prerequisite tracing to root cause.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Tool design complete \u2192 automation gate enabled \u2192 artifact regeneration triggered on PR merge\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T16:41:14.127874Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/assemble_graph.py` \u2014 the Tier-1 rebuild script (per `COVERAGE.md`). Reads `docs/workflow-layers/{L0-forks,L1-trace-*,G1..G8}.json` and writes `dh-workflow-graph.json` plus the embedded data block in `dh-workflow-explorer.html`. Cannot meaningfully rebuild the T5/review-synthesizer topology until L0 (forks), L1 (traces), and G4 (concurrency/dispatch) are re-extracted from `multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` and `agents/review-synthesizer.md` \u2014 the assembler only reflects what's already in the layer JSON.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/merge_layer.py` \u2014 merges extraction fragments into a layer JSON file idempotently (owns exactly 3 responsibilities per `plan/architect-dh-workflow-extractor-system.md` \u00a74.2, a plan-storage doc that does not exist as a file in this repo \u2014 architect spec was apparently never persisted). Part of the not-yet-wired redesign; no caller invokes it yet.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/enumerate_scope.py` \u2014 deterministic BFS crawl of the in-scope file set for extraction (ADR-1). Also part of the redesign; exists but is not invoked by anything (its intended caller, `dh-extract-file.js`, does not exist anywhere in the repo).\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-explorer.html` \u2014 Cytoscape.js viewer that renders `dh-workflow-graph.json`. Will keep showing the stale 4-worker topology with no staleness indicator to the viewer.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_assemble_graph.py`, `plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` \u2014 test the assembler's gap-edge/merge logic itself, not the specific stale data; unaffected by this item unless the assembler's code changes.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor-reducer.md` \u2014 Sonnet verifier agent for the redesigned ensemble pipeline. References `reduce.py` (exists, owned by plugin-creator), `docs/workflow-layers/extraction-rules.json` (exists), and a `dh-extract-file.js` dispatcher (does NOT exist anywhere in the repo \u2014 confirmed via repo-wide `find`). This agent is currently unreachable: nothing dispatches it.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` and `plan_ensemble.py` \u2014 owned by the plugin-creator plugin, reused as shared infrastructure by the DH extractor design (confirmed by prior agent-memory, see below). SAM task T07 in `Pe7547575-dh-workflow-extractor-system.yaml` proposes upstream changes to `reduce.py` (slug-normalized heading keys + a `cross_group` signal) gated by a backward-compat protocol \u2014 status `in-progress`, started `2026-06-20`, stalled roughly 2 months as of today (2026-08-29). This is a live cross-plugin coupling: a schema change to `reduce.py`'s output would affect both plugins.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md` \u2014 authoritative update-process manifest. Names L0, L1, and G4 as the layers a dispatch/topology change like this one requires re-extracting, and states re-extraction is \\\"pending redesign\\\" pointing at the PRD.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/L0-forks.json`, `L1-trace-*.json` (4 files), `G4-concurrency.json` \u2014 stale source layer data feeding the assembler; none reflect `review-synthesizer` or the T5 stage.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` \u2014 still lists `workflow-extractor-worker`, `workflow-extractor-reducer`, and (implicitly) `workflow-extractor` as canonical agents. Prior agent-memory (dated 2026-06-16, see below) already flagged this as a known-stale inconsistency: the worker and base agent files do not exist under `agents/`, only `workflow-extractor-reducer.md` does.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-trace-methodology.md` \u2014 full extraction protocol / ensemble pipeline methodology referenced by both `COVERAGE.md` and the `workflow-extraction.md` rule.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/graph-schema.md` \u2014 schema consumed by `assemble_graph.py`; documents the node/edge shapes rendered by the explorer.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-system-model.html` \u2014 links out to the Workflow Explorer; itself classified `generated, not authoritative behavioral contract` in the purpose-audit manifest, and its own Phases 3\u20136 are listed `PENDING` in `COVERAGE.md`'s gap table (pre-existing, unrelated gap).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/meta-workflow-graph-refresh/SKILL.md` \u2014 entry-point skill; points readers at `COVERAGE.md` and `workflow-trace-methodology.md`, inheriting the \\\"pending redesign\\\" blocker rather than stating it directly.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md` \u2014 Draft v4 PRD for the redesigned extraction ensemble. Explicitly self-labeled: \\\"Authority: Historical design snapshot. Tool-call forms below are captured extraction patterns, not current executable signatures.\\\"\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plans/Pe7547575-dh-workflow-extractor-system.yaml` \u2014 the actual 23-task SAM plan implementing the PRD. 22 of 23 tasks are `not-started`; only T07 is `in-progress` (and stalled). Critically, T20 (rewrite `.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` for the new SessionStart/`dh-extract-file.js` design) and T23 (update `dh-workflow-explorer.html` for new node/edge types) are both `not-started` \u2014 the redesign is incomplete even on paper, not just unbuilt.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/audits/purpose-audit-reference-manifest.yaml` \u2014 classifies `dh-workflow-graph.json`, `dh-workflow-explorer.html`, `dh-system-model.html`, `assemble_graph.py`, and `docs/workflow-layers/**` as `generated, not authoritative behavioral contract`. Staleness here does not violate a documented behavioral contract, but confirms these are known-derivative artifacts rather than hand-maintained sources of truth.\\n\\n### Configuration/CI\\n\\n- `biome.json` \u2014 excludes `dh-workflow-graph.json` from formatting (machine-generated).\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 excludes `dh-workflow-graph.json` from a hook pattern, with a comment noting it's machine-generated minified JSON.\\n- No CI workflow validates graph freshness: `grep -rl \\\"dh-workflow-graph\\\\|workflow-extractor\\\\|assemble_graph\\\" .github/workflows/` returns zero hits across all 9 workflow files. Nothing will fail a build or PR check over this staleness.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` (~line 441\u2013444) \u2014 instructs contributors to run `/dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh` after adding skills/agents or changing dispatch logic (exactly PR #3207's change class), but does not itself warn that re-extraction is currently blocked pending the redesign.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` \u2014 path-scoped rule (`docs/workflow-layers/**`, `docs/workflow-trace-methodology.md`). States extraction \\\"agent roles are pending redesign\\\" pointing at the PRD, and separately flags that the existing L0\u2013G8 layer data (collected 2026-06-08) is itself unverified \u2014 \\\"useful starting hypotheses, not ground truth.\\\" Even a manual re-extraction attempt today would start from data already flagged as suspect.\\n- `.claude/agent-memory/dh-impact-analyst/project_workflow_extractor_cross_plugin_pattern.md` and `.claude/agent-memory/dh-impact-analyst/MEMORY.md` \u2014 prior impact-analyst memory already documents this exact subsystem's fragility: fabricated `workflow-extractor-worker`/`workflow-extractor.md` agents were removed by a prior commit, `KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` was already known-stale as of 2026-06-16, and the cross-plugin `reduce.py`/`plan_ensemble.py` dependency was already flagged as a risk. Directly relevant precedent for this item.\\n- `.claude/agent-memory/dh-service-docs-maintainer/dh-mcp-cli-docs.md` \u2014 notes a second, independent gap in the same assembler pipeline: the extraction rule for MCP tool nodes only recognizes `mcp__...(...)` call syntax, not the CLI form (`uv run .../cli.py <command>`) \u2014 relevant if re-extraction work touches the same extraction rules.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- Human developers and AI agents consulting `dh-workflow-explorer.html` or `dh-system-model.html` for the current review-dispatch topology will see 4 workers, not 5 (missing `review-synthesizer`/T5), with no staleness indicator in the UI itself.\\n- No downstream automated system (CI, MCP server, hook) reads `dh-workflow-graph.json` programmatically for gating \u2014 confirmed via the CI grep above. Consumption is human-facing only, via the explorer. So no automated pipeline breaks; only documentation/comprehension accuracy is at risk.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [x] Producers identified (`assemble_graph.py`, `merge_layer.py`, `enumerate_scope.py`)\\n- [x] Consumers identified (`dh-workflow-explorer.html`, `workflow-extractor-reducer.md`, assembler tests)\\n- [x] Cross-plugin dependency identified (plugin-creator's `reduce.py`/`plan_ensemble.py`; stalled upstream task T07)\\n- [x] CI/config checked \u2014 confirmed no gating step exists\\n- [x] Prior agent-memory checked \u2014 matching precedent found and reconciled (this exact subsystem's fragility was already documented 2026-06-16)\\n- [ ] Orchestrating dispatcher (`dh-extract-file.js`) confirmed absent \u2014 re-extraction cannot proceed until this (and its T09/T10-class wiring) is built\\n- [ ] `workflow-extractor-worker` agent confirmed absent despite `KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` still listing it as canonical \u2014 pre-existing known-stale doc, not newly discovered by this item\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #3207 review thread (chatgpt-codex-connector), addressed during rebase on 2026-08-24\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d8564b98d296d0267d1a683dc6a050d9d83c4f495cc00f25c8ad337ed4b4f0c4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRSg5sA\"}"}